module src::services::projects::project_item_symbol_promotion;

// Port of squalr-engine/src/services/projects/project_item_symbol_promotion.rs:
// the promote-symbol coordinator — builds `ProjectSymbolClaim`s from project
// items, dedupes them against the project symbol catalog, mirrors them into
// the module-root struct layouts, and rewrites the promoted items' addresses.
//
// Respelling notes:
// - `EngineExecutionContext` resolves to the unprivileged port's dual context
//   `(engine_unprivileged_state, engine_bindings)`; the upstream
//   mpsc-channel + callback dispatch of privileged commands becomes the
//   caller-owned `PrivilegedResponseMailbox` on `dispatch_privileged_command`.
// - `HashSet<String>` visited sets resolve to `SymbolLayoutVisitSet` (bounded
//   64) from symbol_layout_size_resolver; `BTreeMap<String, u64>` module size
//   hints resolve to a bounded name+size list with max-upsert; `Vec` carriers
//   resolve to bounded lists (conflicts 16, claims 64, replacements 64,
//   spans 64).
// - Upstream mutates a CLONED `existing_symbol_claims` vec then writes it
//   back through `set_symbol_claims`; this port mutates the catalog's claims
//   in place (find/add/set_at). The end state is identical — the catalog IS
//   the claim list — and in-place preserves the upstream dedup scope, since
//   the ported `deduplicate_display_name` reads the catalog's claims
//   directly (its signature carries no pending-claims vec).
// - `ensure_module_root_struct_layout`/`materialize_struct_layout_definition`
//   are catalog methods upstream; they need `EngineUnprivilegedState` for
//   unit sizes, which the api package cannot see — they land here, upstream
//   naming kept.
// - `SymbolicFieldSpan`/`ContainingChildStructLayout` are upstream private
//   structs — bounded list carriers here.
// - `source.pointer_offsets` metadata: upstream serde_json-serializes the
//   offset segments; there is no JSON substrate in the pin's library, so the
//   port renders segments textually (`0x…` offsets / `symbol:name`).
// - `existing_locator_display`: upstream `ProjectSymbolLocator::to_string(locator)` — the port
//   stores the locator key bytes (the only textual locator surface).
// - `SymbolicStructDefinition::from_str` has no port (the api parser only
//   exists for fields) — `estimate_symbol_type_size_in_bytes` drops that arm;
//   documented deviation.

